    "notes": "Sheet is a 230V AC power distribution schedule for a yacht (SWS 108' Gelliceaux). Main AC DB panel on left feeds numbered breakers (#1-#9) each protected by CTs and earth-leakage breakers, branching to sub-panels/loads across the sheet in columns (Q1-Q38 rating/load rows). Right side has pump control connector blocks (labelled as SWITCH-like harness interfaces with many pins, e.g. RM35JA32MW, 3UG4621-1AW30) feeding pump motors, plus small relay/timer modules (Re1/T1) and terminal strip taps (21-24, 25-32) routing status/monitoring signals to XA40 and a passage-panel terminal strip via multi-core cable MU-XX. Bottom center has an INVERTER 205KW power conversion unit bridging 24VDC and 230VAC buses feeding remaining Q34-Q38 loads. Bottom left has CTA 1-13 text tag legend all mapping to QI-POWER-485. Some breaker/load text at far right (Q33, Q37, Q38) illegible/blank at this resolution - appears unlabeled or spare. Title block bottom right per standard format.",
